    whyItMatters: "Genetic engineering is one of the most consequential technologies of the modern era, with applications ranging from insulin production to disease-resistant crops. In the HSC, you must understand the process — including the roles of restriction enzymes, ligase, plasmids, and transformation — and discuss both the benefits and ethical concerns.",
    scenario: "A biotechnology student traced the steps used to produce human growth hormone in bacteria. Scientists isolated the human growth hormone gene from human DNA, cut it with restriction enzymes that left 'sticky ends'. A bacterial plasmid was cut with the same enzyme, creating compatible sticky ends. The human gene was inserted into the plasmid using DNA ligase, and the recombinant plasmid was introduced into bacteria, which then replicated and produced the human hormone in large quantities.",
