    scenario: "A researcher studying HIV infection explained why the virus was so difficult for the immune system to combat. HIV selectively infected and destroyed helper T cells (CD4+ cells), which were responsible for coordinating both the B cell antibody response and the cytotoxic T cell response. As helper T cell numbers declined, the entire adaptive immune response was weakened, leaving the patient vulnerable to opportunistic infections that a healthy immune system would easily suppress.",
    example: '"HIV destroys helper T cells, which is why AIDS patients can\'t fight off infections that would be trivial for a healthy immune system — the entire coordinating hub of the adaptive response is being dismantled."',
